/ref 17592186204880 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204149 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186204881 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204149 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204149 #edb/ref 1045 "Sums of Squares" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204149 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186204875 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204149 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050406 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204149 #edb/ref 1050 900.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204149 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "3ca1fe5c-e3e2-5af9-bb9f-82c8c2f00317" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204445 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186202606 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204445 #edb/ref 1069 "q-251491" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204445 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204445 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider two sets of $25$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{25},$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{25}.$ You are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{25}{x}_{i}=250, \\\\  & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{25}{y}_{i}=265, \\\\  & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{25}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}=3\\,625.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, ${S}_{xy}=$\n{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204445 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d5e13c72-a4ef-5310-a416-6c1b8d1065c7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204445 #edb/ref 1074 "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ the statistic ${S}_{xy}$ be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}-\\frac{1}{n}({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given statistics in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & =3\\,625-\\frac{1}{25}(250)(265) \\\\  & =3\\,625-2\\,650 \\\\  & =975.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204875 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186204876 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204875 #edb/ref 1061 226927 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204875 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "780a886e-f7ec-5134-8c19-6ef13b7e6958" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204875 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186205125 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204876 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186204877 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204876 #edb/ref 1061 226928 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204876 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c4508f2d-5b01-5156-a636-efc40f9518ac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204876 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186204008 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204877 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186204878 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204877 #edb/ref 1061 226931 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204877 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b96fcd87-a442-5e10-907a-17ae7bf45eef" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204877 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186204009 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204878 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186204879 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204878 #edb/ref 1061 226934 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204878 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d1fb1eb8-ff7c-5cd3-b9e5-580d6a2360ac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204878 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186205126 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204879 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186204880 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204879 #edb/ref 1061 226935 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204879 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "88b4bb82-3260-512d-b14c-8e8a43f1aaa4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204879 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186204010 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204880 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186204881 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204880 #edb/ref 1061 226938 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204880 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9f0e96ac-7d59-5c73-8d5d-f336df384031" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204880 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186204011 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204881 #edb/ref 1061 226941 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204881 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ddc81863-5abf-5730-bfbc-1afae5ed8857" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204881 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186205148 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205125 #edb/ref 1064 "Given a data set $x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n,$ we know that its variance, which we may denote as $\\sigma_x^2,$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\sigma_x^2 = \\dfrac1n \\sum_{i=1}^n (x_i - \\overline x)^2\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overline x$ is the mean of $x.$ \n\nThe summation term\n\n$$\nS_{xx} = \\sum_{i=1}^n (x_i - \\overline x)^2\n$$\n\nis known as a **sum of squares** and is denoted $S_{xx}.$ As we'll see, this quantity often appears in statistical analysis, so giving it a separate notation is useful.\n\nSimilarly, if we have a data set $y_1, y_2, \\ldots, y_n,$ then we define\n\n$$\nS_{yy} =  \\sum_{i=1}^n (y_i - \\overline y)^2.\n$$\n\nNow, suppose we have the bivariate data set\n\n$$\n(x_1, y_1), \\qquad (x_2, y_2),\\qquad \\ldots, \\qquad (x_n, y_n).\n$$\n\nThen, the covariance is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Cov}(x,y) =  \\dfrac1n\\sum_{i=1}^n (x_i - \\overline x)(y_i - \\overline y)\n$$\n\nand we may define $S_{xy}$ as\n\n$$\nS_{xy} = \\sum_{i=1}^n (x_i - \\overline{x})(y_i - \\overline{y}).\n$$\n\nFinally, we can define the variance and covariance in terms of $S_{xx}, S_{yy},$ and $S_{xy}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{x}^{2} & =\\frac{{S}_{xx}}{n},\\,{\\sigma }_{y}^{2}=\\frac{{S}_{yy}}{n},\\,\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{{S}_{xy}}{n}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205125 #edb/ref 1065 10575 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205125 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "f7e454c5-fb32-5adc-b4bd-0eb93ccd4ce7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205125 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205126 #edb/ref 1064 "Calculating $S_{xx}, S_{yy},$ and $S_{xy}$ using their definitions can be cumbersome. Thankfully, we have the following shortcut formulas:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2}-\\frac{1}{n}{({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})}^{2} \\\\ {S}_{yy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}^{2}-\\frac{1}{n}{({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i})}^{2} \\\\ {S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}-\\frac{1}{n}({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe'll prove these at the end of the lesson." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205126 #edb/ref 1065 10576 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205126 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "c497f58a-e56b-5fde-9a53-c8553e8dcbcf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205126 #edb/ref 1067 "Shortcut Formulas" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205148 #edb/ref 1064 "We wish to prove that\n\n![](images/6e/6e45f9e7a628f5275b3da6d56cbf02f7b36a058ed330f92176c50a3820a950d7.svg)\n\nWe start with the definition of ![](images/35/3596d7dd81777a4d3334085c1b707f68c8ade782b3a9b435ec815b5b9cd718c1.svg)\n\n![](images/47/4729fc0ed523938607245027c4e2354b97d5c70fc12faba653f826123ce7e116.svg)\n\nFirst, we expand the binomial:\n\n![](images/7f/7fbf3c03450c32af2eac42db8a67fa185cb7a88a48b9f55a22b21b8f15bbc8d0.svg)\n\nDistributing the summation, we have\n\n![](images/07/079466ea370445b1274143031c8ddf28d09569757c05a439ff967d6c5e835dc5.svg)\n\nNow, since ![](images/41/413a174ed8eab4231f8960e47693592ddfebbf73fbad3284ccd11c5233076316.svg) and ![](images/ed/ed33df1256b85619e6408ee6014ce30223f75c5df8ca599ec4f4c99fe0f293ac.svg) are constants, we can write this as\n\n![](images/8a/8a12508a4a5e1890cac8b9814966b826dd67c7c89977e2fcb223b859ee016464.svg)\n\nNext, we use the following results:\n\n![](images/de/de94aad0fc385eebb157d4a4fec1f763ef02190462eacf53f27de4769f3ae42d.svg)\n\nThis gives\n\n![](images/98/98de282215c98d829d9d7984442773a2086ca640b29542382a060826270489ae.svg)\nas required.\n\nThe proofs for ![](images/40/409afd81c4ea93a33782db88296b0a9f7e9e982a14a16274e2ec50739d363f14.svg) and ![](images/02/02f6f964f68603338fc2cbe3b6d3be2b6af947670bec73bc8810b14208e1090e.svg) are similar." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205148 #edb/ref 1065 10852 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205148 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "7dab2448-da48-5100-9373-89c074ae5326" #edb/ref 17592186045